    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=0674ba22-8f97-458a-80c0-91217826b19b&ccId=9151465763873_19553&jobId=9200882629019_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing (2 Positions Available)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-02-12\n\nLocation: Lakewood\n\nThe Department of Nursing seeks full time faculty Assistant Professor  to support an expanding nursing major.  The candidate should enjoy teaching above all other aspects of academia and must bring creative pedagogy to the classroom.  He or she will develop/revise curriculum and coordinate clinical laboratory experiences in Adult Health and other specialty  courses as needed.  This is a full time tenure-track 12 month position in the -Hackensack Meridian Health School of Nursing beginning Summer 2026 Essential Functions: Integrate the Mercy core values of respect, integrity, compassion, justice and service in all aspects of interaction. Teach Adult Health and other courses in the curriculum as needed    in a BSN, ABSN and DEMSN program using active learning strategies.  Experience in a specialty area such as Behavioral Health, Maternal Child, Pediatrics, and/or Community Health is desirable. Conduct learning needs assessment and assessing learning outcomes. Participate in curriculum redesign. Mentor graduates for NCLEX success. Actively participate in regulatory and accreditation processes, including assessment, self-study preparation, and site visit activities.  Develop, implement, and assess the clinical laboratory placements. Integrate QSEN, inter-professional and other emerging competencies into teaching and learning. Advise/mentor students. Participate in departmental, university school service. Collaborate in program development, student recruitment, student remediation, and continuous program assessment and improvement. Regularly participate in course assessment and program assessment and be willing to make improvements in teaching/advising. Engage in scholarly activities including original research, presentations, and publications. Teach at the Lakewood campus, off-site locations, in the evening and weekends and over the summer. Teach in the regular, ABSN and DEMSN program including summer offerings as needed. Collaborate with colleagues in on-going off-site teaching initiatives. Coordinate on campus and off-site clinical learning laboratory activities Investigate innovative technology to enhance the learning environment for students. Communicate with clinical instructors on the required skills and competencies required of students in a changing health care environment. Participate in departmental functions such as lectures, Open House, etc. Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Master’s degree in nursing required/ Doctoral Degree strongly preferred;  Licensed or eligible for licensure as a RN in New Jersey. Knowledge and experience in teaching in the classroom and clinical settings     Prior experience in nursing in the acute care setting  Prior experience in other nursing specialties desirable   Demonstrated evidence of teaching excellence.  Ability or willingness to learn to use instructional technologies effectively is essential; Familiarity with distance learning is desirable.  Commitment to active, learner centered teaching.  Experience assessing learning outcomes in courses and programs. Knowledge of nursing curricular design/assessment and BON and/or CCNE accreditation.  Ability to work collaboratively and cooperatively with students and faculty.  Strong clinical nursing skillset and recent clinical experience preferred. **MUST BE US WORK AUTHORIZED**",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=0674ba22-8f97-458a-80c0-91217826b19b&ccId=9151465763873_19553&jobId=9200863740740_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of School Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-09\n\nLocation: Lakewood\n\nThe successful candidate will primarily teach in the school psychology graduate programs. This individual will teach courses both at the MA/CAGS and Psy.D. level and supervise doctoral dissertations. Essential Functions: Integrate the Mercy core values of respect, compassion, integrity, justice and service in all aspects of interaction. Teach 12 credits per semester in the MA/CAGS and PsyD graduate programs in School Psychology, as well as courses in the undergraduate program in the Psychology and Counseling Department.  Teach in lecture, online, or hybrid modalities. Ability to teach evening courses.  Ability to supervise doctoral dissertations Participate in ongoing data collection and assessments needed to successfully continue NASP accreditation. Collaborate with colleagues regarding course materials (developing or using common syllabi/course outlines). Engage in Scholarly activities Participate in departmental functions such as lectures, Open House, etc. Engage in University-wide and departmental service. Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: A doctorate in School Psychology is required (ABD with a known completion date can be considered). NJ-Certified School Psychologist (or eligible to become a NJ-Certified School Psychologist) Licensed or licensed-eligible Psychologist in the state of NJ Ability to teach a variety of courses in school psychology related to area of interest/expertise  Ability to supervise doctoral dissertations **MUST BE US WORK AUTHORIZED**",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
